          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The ancient cymbals resembled those in use in our day, consisting of two circular concave plates of brass, or other metal, and producing a clanging sound by being struck against each other. Two kinds are supposed to be mentioned in the text. The “loud cymbals” are thought to have…"
      }
